<p>On-page SEO is everything on the page itself that tells Google, and your customers, what it is about. Getting it right is usually cheaper and faster than people expect, because it improves how you use the traffic you already have.</p>

<h2>What is included</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Title tag and meta description rewrites</li>
  <li>A heading structure (H1 to H3) that reflects the page content</li>
  <li>Internal linking between related pages</li>
  <li>Keyword placement that reads naturally, never stuffed</li>
  <li>Content gap filling for thin or missing pages</li>
  <li>Readability improvements for real visitors, not just crawlers</li>
</ul>

<p>The goal is content a real customer finishes reading, because a page that ranks but does not convert is not doing its job.</p>
